            <h2>Step‑by‑Step Journey Experience</h2>
            <p>Planning ahead makes every part of your Detroit-to-Chicago train journey smooth and predictable. From arriving at your departure station to stepping off in Chicago, this section walks you through what to expect at each stage.</p>
            <h2>Arrival at the Station in Detroit</h2>
            <p>Most Wolverine trains depart from Detroit Amtrak Station, located near the city center. Arrive at least 2030 minutes before departure to allow time for ticket checks and boarding directions.</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Stations typically have waiting areas, restrooms, and sometimes kiosks or small cafes.</li>
                <li>Display boards show departure gates and train status.</li>
            </ul>
            <h3>Boarding Process</h3>
            <p>Boarding the Amtrak Wolverine train in Detroit is straightforward. Platforms are usually announced 1520 minutes before departure, and staff are available to guide passengers. Seats are clearly marked, so finding your spot is simple, and there are no airport-style security checks, making the process faster and more relaxed.</p>
            <h3>Onboard Experience</h3>
            <p>The Detroit-to-Chicago train offers a comfortable, productive travel experience. Amtrak’s Wolverine service provides:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Spacious seating with ample legroom</li>
                <li>Overhead luggage storage and designated luggage areas</li>
                <li>Quiet cars for working or relaxing</li>
                <li>Panoramic views of Michigan, Indiana, and Illinois landscapes</li>
                <li>Amenities such as Wi-Fi (on select services), power outlets, and food options</li>
