            <h2>Arrival in Chicago</h2>
            <p>Trains arrive at Chicago Union Station, located in the city center, making access to downtown hotels, offices, and attractions very convenient. The station is well-equipped with amenities, including restaurants and shops, and offers easy access to public transportation, including buses, taxis, and Metra trains.</p>
            <h2>Tips to Save Money on This Route</h2>
            <p>Traveling from Detroit to Chicago doesn’t have to be expensive. A few smart strategies can help you find better fares without compromising comfort or convenience. Prices on this route vary depending on timing, train type, and booking window.</p>
            <h3>Plan Ahead for Better Price Options</h3>
            <p>Booking your tickets early is one of the most effective ways to save money. Amtrak often offers lower prices for passengers who reserve seats several weeks in advance. Early planning also provides more options for departure times and seating preferences.</p>
            <h3>Travel During Off-Peak Hours</h3>
            <p>Choosing departure times outside peak hours can reduce ticket costs. Midday trains often offer lower prices and fewer crowds compared to early morning or evening departures, which are more popular with business travelers.</p>
            <h3>Stay Flexible with Your Travel Plans</h3>
            <p>Flexibility in your travel schedule can help you save money and find the most convenient options. Being open to slightly different departure times or train types can make a noticeable difference in fare prices.</p>
